I’ll try to answer them here

# [_Sign in if user lacks access to Apple Account_|https://support.apple.com/en-us/102571]_: am I correct that the user would be able to use their phone number to log in to the Bolt app if they lack access to AppleID or unlink Sign in with Apple function?_

{color:#008da6}      Apple Auth is just an option, and phone option will always be there {color}

# _If the account does not exist, am I correct that we will request name and email from Apple and then create an account based on the retrieved info from Apple (eg linked to AppleID)?_
## Is this correct that the user will not be able to specify their name or email which are separate from AppleID info?
{color:#008da6}User can change their name in the Profile later{color}
## What if user does not approve accessing this info? What are our next steps?
### Apple states: _You can request to receive the user’s information, such as name and email address. If the user approves accessing this information, your authorization request includes the requested information._
{color:#008da6}Basically from the modal perspective user giving use name and email explicitly through the Apple. If any error in the process, we will not be linking the Apple account on our side and give the user another option{color}
# What will happen if the user changes their email address or name in the app after binding Apple sign-in? Will it ruin Sign in with Apple logic as we would use email address from AppleID?
{color:#008da6}Social logins should be linked by externalId, and not by email or Name{color}
# How will we check that the account is bound to socials? Is this just checking on our side that a certain app has a bound social account or any other flow via Apple?
{color:#008da6}We will check binding from our side for the user.{color}
# Will we prevent duplicate accounts as advised here if we check whether the app is bound to socials?[https://developer.apple.com/documentation/sign_in_with_apple/authenticating-users-with-sign-in-with-apple#Send-information-to-app-servers-and-verify-tokens|https://developer.apple.com/documentation/sign_in_with_apple/authenticating-users-with-sign-in-with-apple#Send-information-to-app-servers-and-verify-tokens|smart-link]
{color:#008da6}Currently if the already existing user attempts to login with Apple and we cannot match the Apple account to our user, we will ask the user phone number to authenticate with it and then link it.{color}
{color:#008da6}With some updates on Identity side we will be able to sign up the user right away and go through the Phoneless flow, where we still ask the number later and then give the user the choice left it as new account or merge it (link) with the previous one{color}

Hey! Dmitry’s responses make sense to me. I just want to elaborate a bit on some points:


# _How will we check that the account is bound to socials? Is this just checking on our side that a certain app has a bound social account or any other flow via Apple?_
{color:#008da6}_We will check binding from our side for the user._{color}

When user taps “Login with Apple”, or “Link Apple account”, we receive an external ID from Apple. That ID is always the same for that Apple account for apps published by Bolt (it will not be the same if that user is trying to log into Uber, for example). When they try to login, we check if that specific external ID is linked to any Bolt account.

# _Will we prevent duplicate accounts as advised here if we check whether the app is bound to socials?_[https://developer.apple.com/documentation/sign_in_with_apple/authenticating-users-with-sign-in-with-apple#Send-information-to-app-servers-and-verify-tokens|https://developer.apple.com/documentation/sign_in_with_apple/authenticating-users-with-sign-in-with-apple#Send-information-to-app-servers-and-verify-tokens|smart-link]
{color:#008da6}_Currently if the already existing user attempts to login with Apple and we cannot match the Apple account to our user, we will ask the user phone number to authenticate with it and then link it._{color}
{color:#008da6}_With some updates on Identity side we will be able to sign up the user right away and go through the Phoneless flow, where we still ask the number later and then give the user the choice left it as new account or merge it (link) with the previous one_{color}

The scope of this project is just Login with Apple, not registration. All registration will be done via phone number, so there should be no account duplication at this point.

