Hi [~accountid:62d7b457807cf6f78ca9d117] thanks for looping me in. I’ll say more than legal arguments based on contracts this comes from an industry practice (the explanation is below). However, in my opinion it is unfortunate it happened tho, and we probably should look into the logic for routing payments or extend pre auths in RO if there are too many of these cases ([~accountid:712020:c152e340-503c-4822-bf8e-89c9f6cffb24]). Its not a good customer experience.  

The customer should have the funds available in their bank account by now, and I am not sure what kind of explanation she is expecting, if any, but if an explanation is needed, then:

{color:#0747a6}”To ensure the validity of payment methods and to confirm that sufficient funds are available for the anticipated fare, as part of standard industry practice Bolt places a temporary pre-authorization hold before a ride begins to confirm the validity of the payment method and ensure sufficient funds are available. This is not an actual charge but a pending transaction. Once the ride is completed, the hold is either released or adjusted to match the final fare. This practice is outlined in our {color}[{color:#0747a6}Terms and Conditions{color}|https://bolt.eu/en/legal/terms-for-riders/]{color:#0747a6} under {color}{color:#0747a6}*Section 3.1*{color}{color:#0747a6}:{color}

{color:#0747a6}_"Puteți efectua plata pentru serviciile de transport cu cardul, dar și prin alte metode de plată (de exemplu: Bolt Business), care necesită activarea prealabilă a funcției din aplicația Bolt."_{color}

{color:#0747a6}In your case, the final ride price exceeded the initially authorized amount by 0.1 RON. When this occurs, a second authorization is required instead of adjusting the original hold. The first authorization was subsequently released. While Bolt immediately communicates the release of any holds upon completion of a ride, the timing of the release depends on the customer’s bank, and while many financial institutions process these instantly, in some cases, it may take longer. Unfortunately, this is not something Bolt can control. This aspect is also covered in {color}{color:#0747a6}*Section 3.3*{color}{color:#0747a6} of our Terms and Conditions:{color}

{color:#0747a6}_"La efectuarea plăților pentru serviciile de transport alternativ prin intermediul aplicației Bolt, Bolt nu este responsabilă pentru posibilele costuri suportate cu plățile terților (de exemplu: operatori de telecomunicații mobile, comisioane bancare)."_{color}

{color:#0747a6}Our approach to pre-authorization, including handling final fare adjustments, aligns with standard practices and is necessary to ensure a secure and efficient transaction process for both riders and drivers. {color}

{color:#0747a6}While we understand the frustration caused by the temporary unavailability of funds, we assure you that Bolt does not block or hold money beyond the necessary authorization period. These measures ensure that drivers receive due compensation for services rendered and that users have a validated and secure payment method. {color}

{color:#0747a6}Should you require any additional clarification, we remain available to discuss this further.”{color}


If anyone has questions or feedback to the above please let me know.

