I called the Tribunal de Caen (3ème chambre civil): 


*How and when to submit the arguments of defence?* 

* Any time before or at the audience (ideally 2 weeks before);
* Need to respect the disclosure rules and send the arguments to the opposing party as well;
* By post to the address indicated on the notification to attend the hearing. 

*Will the submission of the arguments lead to an anticipated cancellation of the hearing?*

* No - the judge will only take the arguments into consideration at the hearing;
* There is a two month lapse between the audience and the deliberation (le temps pour le juge de se statuer). 

*Do we need a representation during the hearing?*

* for an oral hearing such as this, we do not need a lawyer to represent us, however, a person with an adequate PoA needs to be present to introduce our arguments to the judge. 
* If the claimant does not attend the hearing = the judge will not address the matter, case closed;
* if the defendant does not attend the hearing = the judge may still hear the matter and make a judgement on it. 

