Hi Victoria,

We have planned adjustments in the [Global Event Assessment Tool |https://www.cognitoforms.com/Taxify1/globaleventassessmenttool2]for safety incidents where the provider is the reported (accused) party, during which we will aim to hide the following fields from the {{Investigation}} section, such as:

* {{Occurrence}}
* {{Demerit Decay}}
* {{Deviant Action}}
* {{Reasoning for Deviant Action}}
* Prompt to suspend the provider’s account temporarily until the investigation is completed:
** {{PLACE INVESTIGATIVE SUSPENSION ON ACCUSED PARTY}}
** {{CONFIRM ANY PROVIDER'S BLOCK WITH OPS}}

As a result, the {{Action Required}} and {{Please Confirm That You Have Taken Action According to the Tool's Suggestion}} fields will also not be shown.

This ensures that CS agents who are receiving the report from the eater/courier can investigate the provider-related safety incident with related parties and log the report in the tool, but:

* they won’t be asked to fill out information which they do not have access to view (such as occurrences)
* they won’t be asked to implement temporary account suspensions until the investigation is completed and fault, or no fault has been determined (such as temporary account suspensions)
* they won’t be asked to implement consequential corrective actions (such as temporary consequential suspensions or account terminations)

The changes are currently due to go live in April, however, you will receive an update in Beehive on this once the Assessment Tool and workflow article both are updated.

